/*! \mainpage

The Nuclear Data Interface, NDI, is a C, C++, F77, and F90 callable
library which provides nuclear data to user codes.  NDI solves the
commanded information problem for nuclear data:

\image latex problem.ps "The Commanded Information Frame"
\image html problem.jpg "The Commanded Information Frame"

-# When the user issues request E1 that NDI is required to respond to,
-# if UC!E1 is not sensible according to specification then NDI will
   return and error code,
-# or if the requested data Y1 is not available either explicitly or via
   calculation according to specification NDI will return a warning
   code or else read NDI!Y1,
-# which because the nuclear data has the real world properties,
-# that satisfy the nuclear data requirements,
-# NDI can assign NDI!Y2 according to specification,
-# of the user's data format,
-# resulting in Y2 ~ Y1 as required.

To use NDI:
-# Open a gendir handle
   - optionally set or check the gendir handle state
   - optionally get data from the gendir handle
-# Make a data handle
   - optionally set or check the data handle state
   - optionally get data from the data handle
-# Close the gendir handle

